[
  {
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8b8758ce-a8de-5a9d-9235-b64a7c3961d7",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $4$th column.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "913efa0b-c972-5f01-ac2a-eadf398e0553",
