      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column.",
