      ":question/id": "901651a9-065a-5d37-a273-b626636babe7",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column.",
