    "question": {
      ":question/id": "072ae517-5ad2-5d86-aa6b-241bb3901298",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -6 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -6 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns.",
