    "question": {
      ":question/id": "43832bf2-d03e-54d6-9ce1-104c48b36aff",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $R$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & -2 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -6 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $R$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & -2 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -6 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $3$rd and $5$th columns.",
