    "question": {
      ":question/id": "daa45d6a-ba36-5c8d-b7cf-ce0d7964e285",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & -5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $2$ pivots in the $2$nd and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & -5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $4$th columns.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
